telnet: 
```````Linux-Linux || Linux-Windows

CLI based network protocol and application used to connect to and manage remote computers or network devices (like routers/switches) over TCP/IP

Port: 23

ON SERVER:
````````````
1) Install package:
````````````````````
$ sudo apt install telnetd -y

Edit the config file:
vim /etc/inetd.conf

Go to line & uncomment it:
telnet  stream  tcp  nowait  telnetd  /usr/sbin/tcpd  /usr/sbin/in.telnetd

:wq

2) Start the service:
``````````````````````
$ sudo systemctl restart inetd

$ sudo lsof -i:23

3) Access the remote machine via telnet:
`````````````````````````````````````````
$ telnet x.x.x.x

Trying 192.168.81.25...
Connected to 192.168.81.25.
Escape character is '^]'.

Linux 6.11.0-26-generic (server06) (pts/1)

server06 login: username
password: *******


ON CLIENT:
```````````
Install client side package:

$ sudo apt install telnet -y



